---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import WaitlistForm from '../components/WaitlistForm.astro';
---
<Base title="Our Story" description="Why HaulQ exists, and why we build it fast.">
  <!-- HERO, dark -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-ink text-white">
    <div class="hq-stripes absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-20 pt-20 sm:pt-28">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand">Our story</p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.03] sm:text-6xl">
        Work on the business.<br /><span class="text-brand">Not in it.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-300">
        Every hour you spend scrolling a load board, retyping a rate confirmation, or chasing a
        broker for a check is an hour spent running the business, not growing it. HaulQ automates
        that work, so growing it doesn't have to wait.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE PROBLEM, white -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-20">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">The job ate the business</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-slate">
      Maybe you negotiate the rate, drive the load, upload the paperwork, and call the broker to
      ask where the check is, all yourself. Maybe your team splits that across dispatch, safety
      and the back office instead. Either way, the same load gets typed into a new system at every
      step, whether you're running one truck or fifty.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-slate">
      HaulQ moves with the load instead of starting over. Whoever's turn it is next, you, a
      dispatcher, or someone in accounting, already has what came before. The judgment about which
      load to run, or which broker to trust, still stays with you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- SPEED, warm tint -->
  <section class="border-y border-brand-100 bg-brand-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">Speed is the whole point</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-slate">A small carrier can't wait for a slow quarter. Neither can we.</p>
      <ol class="mt-12 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">
        {[
          ['What you need, without the wait', 'Tell us what’s slowing you down, and we build the fix in weeks. You’re using it, not waiting on a promise.'],
          ['One record, not seven tools stapled together', 'Your load, your broker and your truck live in one place. Enter something once, and every tool you use already has it.'],
          ['Built with carriers, not around them', 'We’re not stopping at what’s here today. Every tool we add next comes from a carrier already running HaulQ, so it plugs into the same load, broker and truck you already have on file. Adding a new tool never means starting over or logging into another app.'],
        ].map(([title, body], i) => (
          <li class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6">
            <span class="display text-sm font-bold text-brand">0{i + 1}</span>
            <h3 class="mt-2 display text-xl font-semibold">{title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate">{body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-20">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">Get early access</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate">
      Tell us what you run and we will let you know as products go live.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 shadow-lg shadow-ink/5 sm:p-8">
      <WaitlistForm />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
